# state: first-run   (recorded on a disk with no save for the title (NOTES.md E); lane.savestate433)
# Crash Bandicoot: The Wrath of Cortex (56550003). No profile step: NEW GAME
# is always the first item and asks only for a name. PLAYED by nav.py on the
# Nova, 2026-09-29 19:43 PDT (lane.titleroutes session 37, HELD; nav session
# crash-wrath-of-cortex.first-run-20260929T194316).
#
# Boot with no input (scratch/replay/bootwatch-194127): copyright and
# publisher logos 6-19 s, NEW GAME / LOAD GAME from ~26 s to ~52 s after
# launch, then a "DEMO" level that plays itself (NOT gameplay).
#
# A on NEW GAME opens a name entry with "CRASH" filled in and DONE
# highlighted; A accepts it. Then a load, the intro cutscene (START skips
# it, ~22 s after the name), a load into the warp room, and a second
# cutscene on the warp room's monitor (still running 21 s after the first
# skip; START skips it). A START after that cutscene would open the pause
# menu, so the second START keeps the nav session's spacing.
#
# Gameplay is the warp room hub, not a level: the stick walked Crash across
# the floor and turned him (frames 015-017). The hub is lighter to render
# than a level, so its fps is an upper bound on the title's.
wait 5.0
shot boot
wait 27.0
shot title
mark title
press A 150
wait 4.0
shot name
mark name
press A
wait 22.0
shot intro
press START 150
wait 28.0
shot hub-cutscene
press START 150
wait 5.0
shot hub
mark gameplay
#
# The play loop walks toward the camera and side to side, and presses no
# button: Crash starts in front of the LOAD/SAVE monitor, and the first
# version of this loop (stick up plus A) walked him back into it and opened
# the Load/Save menu (scratch/replay/crash-wrath-of-cortex-194543/zz-end.png).
axis LY max
wait 1.5
axis LY mid
repeat forever {
    axis LX max
    wait 1.5
    axis LX mid
    axis LY max
    wait 0.5
    axis LY mid
    axis LX min
    wait 1.5
    axis LX mid
    axis LY min
    wait 0.4
    axis LY mid
}
